<title>NETHERLANDS: SGS Europe cocoa stock estimates up at end-March.</title>
<headline>SGS Europe cocoa stock estimates up at end-March.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>SGS Warehouse Services gave the following estimates of cocoa in store as of the end of March/early April. All figures in tonnes.</p>
<p>			Total    Of which for the buffer stock</p>
<p>AMSTERDAM	 636,000    33,799.846 (inc 4,425.231 forw sales)</p>
<p>HAMBURG/BREMEN  152,100    15,508.418</p>
<p>ANTWERP	   105,640     1,449.828 (all forw sales)</p>
<p>UK (ALL PORTS)   65,700     1,799.447 (inc 1,799.447 forw sales)</p>
<p>ROTTERDAM	  16,250     8,197.379 (inc 2,092.783 forw sales)</p>
<p>The data give the following changes to month-earlier levels:</p>
<p>AMSTERDAM	 UP  64,000	HAMBURG/BREMEN   UP  15,100</p>
<p>ANTWERP	   UP   8,581	UK (ALL PORTS)   UP   6,515</p>
<p>ROTTERDAM	 UP   1,550</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
